  "goodToKnow": "Die Beweislast is the burden of proof: Die Beweislast trägt der Kläger. In criminal law, the principle in dubio pro reo, im Zweifel für den Angeklagten, means the state must prove guilt. In consumer law, there's a Beweislastumkehr: in the first year after purchase, it's assumed a defect existed at delivery, so the seller must prove otherwise. It has no plural."
